and <italic>HOXB4</italic> was the most significant with a positive correlation qFDR&#x0200a;&#x0003d;&#x0200a;2.21&#x000d7;10<sup>&#x02212;19</sup>. The most significant negative correlation was between <italic>miR-98</italic> and <italic>SERBP1</italic> (qFDR&#x0200a;&#x0003d;&#x0200a;3.97&#x000d7;10<sup>&#x02212;7</sup>), which was ranked 111<sup>th</sup> of the most significant pairs. <xref ref-type="table" rid="pone-0005878-t002"><bold>Table 2</bold></xref> lists top 20 most significant positive and top 20 negative correlation pairs.</p><table-wrap id="pone-0005878-t002" position="float"><object-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pone.0005878.t002</object-id><label>Table 2</label><caption><title>Top 20 miRNA-mRNA pairs (based on correlation qFDR values).</title></caption><graphic id="pone-0005878-t002-2" xlink:href="pone.0005878.t002"/><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" alternate-form-of="pone-0005878-t002-2"><colgroup span="1"><col align="left" span="1"/><col align="center" span="1"/><col align="center" span="1"/><col align="center" span="1"/><col align="center" span="1"/><col align="center" span="1"/><col align="center" span="1"/><col align="center" span="1"/></colgroup><thead><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">miRNAs</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">mRNA genes</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">r</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">p</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Bonferroni-corrected p</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Correlation qFDR</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Co-localization</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td colspan="8" align="left" rowspan="1"><bold>Top 20 positively correlated pairs</bold></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">miR-10a</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">HOXB4</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.823</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" co